      "left": {
        "pageNumber": 21,
        "runningHead": "CH. 11 • IOS SOS MODE & USB LOCKDOWN",
        "content": "<div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Effaceable Storage & Lockdown Features:</strong> Apple <strong>Effaceable Storage</strong> is a dedicated non-volatile <strong>NAND</strong> block storing the DKEK. Android <strong>FRP (Factory Reset Protection)</strong> prevents setup after wipe without original Google account credentials. iOS <strong>Lockdown Mode</strong> provides extreme device hardening against mercenary spyware.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Chapter 11 • Device Triage & Biometric Hardening</span>\n      <h2>iOS SOS Mode, USB Restricted Mode & Biometric Locks</h2>\n    </div>\n    <p>Modern mobile operating systems include anti-forensic safeguards that trigger during seizure:</p>\n\n    <h3>iOS Biometric Disablement (SOS Mode)</h3>\n    <p>In Apple iOS, pressing the Power (Side) button <strong>five times rapidly</strong> (or holding Power + Volume button until the Emergency SOS slider appears) immediately <strong>disables Touch ID and Face ID</strong>! Once triggered, the device reverts to requiring the alphanumeric passcode, and biometrics cannot unlock the phone.</p>\n\n    <h3>iOS USB Restricted Mode</h3>\n    <p>Introduced in iOS 11.4.1+, <strong>USB Restricted Mode</strong> disables data communications over the Lightning / USB-C port if the iPhone has not been unlocked for more than <strong>1 hour</strong>. The port provides power charging only, blocking forensic hardware dongles until the user passcode is entered!</p>"
      },
      "right": {
        "pageNumber": 22,
        "runningHead": "ANDROID ADBKEY RSA PAIRING",
        "content": "<div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Weaver Engine & APK Signatures:</strong> Android <strong>APK Signature Scheme v2/v3</strong> cryptographically protects the entire <strong>APK</strong> archive as a whole against tampering, unlike legacy <strong>JAR</strong> signing. In Android runtime permissions, <strong>Dangerous Permissions</strong> grant access to sensitive hardware and data (e.g. <code>CAMERA</code>, <code>READ_CONTACTS</code>, <code>ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION</code>) and require explicit user consent at runtime.  In Apple's Secure Enclave, the <strong>Weaver</strong> anti-replay hardware engine prevents offline passcode brute-forcing. In Android packages, <code>classes.dex</code> contains compiled code and <code>AndroidManifest.xml</code> defines permissions and package names.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"legal-dispatch-header\">\n      <span class=\"badge-primary\">Android USB Debugging</span>\n      <h2>RSA Key Authorization & adbkey.pub Pairing</h2>\n    </div>\n    <h3>Android USB Debugging Security</h3>\n    <p>Since Android 4.4.2+, Android requires RSA key authentication for USB Debugging:</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li>When an examiner connects an Android device to a forensic workstation via ADB, the workstation presents its public key (<code>~/.android/adbkey.pub</code>).</li>\n      <li>The phone displays a trust prompt: <em>\"Allow USB debugging?\"</em>. Unless the user taps \"Allow\" on the unlocked screen, ADB commands return <code>unauthorized</code> and data cannot be extracted!</li>\n      <li>Forensic examiners can bypass this if they acquire an already-trusted <code>adbkey</code> from the suspect's seized laptop!</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <div class=\"exam-trap-box\">\n      <strong>Exam Rule on Triage & Locks:</strong> Pressing the power button <strong>5 times</strong> disables Touch ID/Face ID in iOS. <strong>USB Restricted Mode</strong> locks Lightning port data after <strong>1 hour</strong>. ADB requires RSA key authorization from <code>adbkey.pub</code>.\n    </div>\n\n    \n        <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-banner\">\n          <div class=\"spread-quiz-cta-info\">\n            <span style=\"font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 8px;\">🎯</span>\n            <div>\n              <strong style=\"font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--text-heading);\">Test Your Mastery: Spread 11</strong>\n              <div style=\"font-size: 0.74rem; color: var(--text-muted);\">Practice all 10 targeted exam questions (Q101–Q110) on Mobile Triage, SOS Mode & USB Lockdown.</div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <button class=\"btn-tool btn-mcq\" onclick=\"window.openMCQForSpread(10)\" style=\"font-size: 0.8rem; padding: 6px 14px;\">Start Quiz (Q101–Q110) →</button>\n        </div>"
      }
